<section class="cs__sec" aria-labelledby="s8">
  <p class="st-k rv">08 · Reflection</p>
  <h2 class="cs__h rv" id="s8">Designing for trust in AI output</h2>
  <p class="cs__p rv">
    An AI that extracts data is only useful if people believe what it extracts. The most important
    design work was not the parsing itself, but the moments around it: teaching it with a real
    document, and checking its results against the source.
  </p>
  <div class="st-grid st-g2 st-wide">
    <div class="pcard rv">
      <p class="pcard__word">Learning</p>
      <h3 class="pcard__title">Keep people in the loop</h3>
      <p class="pcard__text">
        Putting the source and the result side by side turned validation from a chore into a quick
        check, and made correcting the AI feel natural.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="pcard rv">
      <p class="pcard__word">Growth</p>
      <h3 class="pcard__title">Designing a whole SaaS product</h3>
      <p class="pcard__text">
